# PERSONAL MEMORY NEVER GOES IN THE REPOSITORY.
#
# The default store lives at ./memories, and this repo is intended to go
# public. An imported conversation history is the most personal data on the
# machine -- everything its owner has ever told an AI -- and a store that
# lands in a commit cannot be un-landed: rewriting history moves the visible
# copy, not the copies other people already cloned.
#
# The CODE is the shareable part. The memories are not. Keep the store
# outside the repo entirely (AI_MEMORY_ROOT=~/ai_memory) and treat these
# patterns as a second net, not the first one.
memories/
*.memories/
audit.jsonl
.trash/

# scratch
__pycache__/
*.pyc
out.txt
